---
globs: src/memory/**,src/tools/memory.ts,src/components/MemoryPanel.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

Read `.cursor/skills/agent-memory/SKILL.md` before changing what Jarvis remembers.

- `db.ts` is persistence, `manage.ts` is policy, `text.ts` is the one place text is compared.
  Nothing outside those touches IndexedDB.
- Deleting sets `deletedAt`; it does not remove the row. `readAllRecords` returns the trash too, so
  a new reader has to filter — the model can reach delete and clear through a tool.
- Recall is injected into the system prompt, budgeted by `MAX_RECALL_CHARS`. Growing that budget is
  a prompt change and needs the eval harness, because a longer system prompt has already been
  measured dropping tool use here.
- jsdom has no IndexedDB. `src/test/setup.ts` installs `fake-indexeddb/auto`; without it the tests
  assert against the "not available" path.
- Changing `MemoryRecord` needs `DB_VERSION` bumped and an upgrade path.
